{"id":"pathros","name":"Pathros","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:pathros"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Pathros","text":"The name generally given to Upper Egypt (the Thebaid of the Greeks), as distinguished from Matsor, or Lower Egypt (Isa. 11:11; Jer. 44:1, 15; Ezek. 30:14), the two forming Mizraim. After the destruction of Jerusalem by Nebuchadnezzar, colonies of Jews settled “in the country of Pathros” and other parts of Egypt."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H6624","lemma":"פַּתְרוֹס","xlit":"Pathrôwç","gloss":"Pathros, a part of Egypt","kjv":"Pathros","count":5,"share":1},{"strong":"H776","lemma":"אֶרֶץ","xlit":"ʼerets","gloss":"the earth","kjv":"common, country, earth, field","count":3,"share":0.6}],"verses":["Isa.11.11","Jer.44.1","Jer.44.15","Ezek.29.14","Ezek.30.14"],"related":[{"id":"ar","type":"lexical","strong":"H776","why":"both lead with אֶרֶץ (H776)"},{"id":"armenia","type":"lexical","strong":"H776","why":"both lead with אֶרֶץ (H776)"},{"id":"baal-gad","type":"lexical","strong":"H776","why":"both lead with אֶרֶץ (H776)"},{"id":"canaan","type":"lexical","strong":"H776","why":"both lead with אֶרֶץ (H776)"},{"id":"cattle","type":"lexical","strong":"H776","why":"both lead with אֶרֶץ (H776)"},{"id":"chaldea","type":"lexical","strong":"H776","why":"both lead with אֶרֶץ (H776)"}],"works":[]}
